NOTICE — StreamRig's reduced MapAnything backbone
=================================================

This directory contains a reduced copy of MapAnything v1.0.1 (commit
fde8425513178bb4f89fba9828193e6be3ece248), redistributed under the
Apache License 2.0. See LICENSE in this directory. Upstream repository:
https://github.com/facebookresearch/map-anything . Copyright (c) Meta
Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.

StreamRig uses the frozen MapAnything backbone during data preprocessing to
produce multi-view information-sharing features. The model implementation
(mapanything/models/mapanything/model.py) and the geometry, image-processing,
inference, misc and warnings helpers under mapanything/utils/ are identical
to upstream v1.0.1.

Modifications relative to upstream v1.0.1: the upstream datasets, training
tools, benchmark wrappers, external model implementations, tracking
utilities, visualization helpers, and unrelated model variants were removed.
mapanything/models/__init__.py and mapanything/models/mapanything/__init__.py
were reduced so that the package registry exposes only MapAnything. The
vendored pyproject.toml uses the included README filename, discovers
subpackages, and omits the unused rerun visualization dependency and optional
extras for removed components. No numerical operation was changed.

The backbone still relies on `uniception` and the matching DINOv2-large
weights; StreamRig's README describes the required checkpoint and setup.
